= Waves 7–9 cross-wave audit =

'''State: post-merge cross-wave audit.'''

== Scope ==

This audit covers the three consecutive merged corpus waves completed on 2026-09-19:

* [[BITwiki:Wave 7 context audit|Wave 7 — Machine learning and generalization]]: 15 concepts / 45 reader surfaces.
* [[BITwiki:Wave 8 context audit|Wave 8 — Artificial intelligence and agents]]: 9 concepts / 27 reader surfaces.
* [[BITwiki:Wave 9 context audit|Wave 9 — Systems, complexity, and information]]: 10 concepts / 30 reader surfaces.

Combined scope:

<pre>
34 canonical concepts
102 reader surfaces
Core + Simple + Technical
</pre>

The audit checks the merged <code>main</code> state, cross-wave semantic boundaries, graph connectivity after later concepts became canonical, evidence/provenance quality, and completion bookkeeping.

== Audit method ==

The audit re-runs four editorial layers:

# '''Structural / identity''' — Core identity ownership, derivative identity exemption, controlled Domains, source/depth templates, references, category ownership.
# '''Cross-wave semantics''' — later concepts must not silently redefine earlier ones.
# '''Knowledge-graph recurrence''' — later canonical concepts should be linked from earlier pages when the relationship is explanatory and survives review.
# '''Evidence / provenance''' — especially recent 2024–2026 ML/agent sources, where peer-reviewed work and preprints must not be silently conflated.

The complete repository staging and V2 release gates remain the final machine validation.

