== Finding 1 — later waves were not fully back-linked ==

The primary cross-wave defect was incomplete recurrence after canonicalization.

Waves 7 and 8 were internally linked at release time, but Wave 9 did not yet exist when their Core graphs were finalized.

The missing relationships were reviewed individually rather than mechanically adding every possible edge.

Validated repairs include:

<pre>
Machine learning
 ├→ Artificial intelligence
 └→ Large language model

Generalization (machine learning)
 └→ Robustness

Distribution shift
 ├→ Robustness
 └→ Adaptation (systems)

Spurious correlation
 └→ Robustness

Intelligent agent
 ├→ Feedback
 └→ Adaptation (systems)

AI agent
 ├→ Feedback
 └→ Adaptation (systems)

Planning (artificial intelligence)
 └→ Feedback

Agent memory (artificial intelligence)
 └→ Information

Multi-agent system
 ├→ Network
 └→ Complex system

Autonomous agent (artificial intelligence)
 ├→ Feedback
 └→ Adaptation (systems)
</pre>

These additions preserve non-equivalence:

<pre>
generalization ≠ robustness
distribution shift ≠ adaptation
agent ≠ feedback loop
multi-agent system ≠ network
multi-agent system ≠ complex system
memory ≠ information
</pre>

Links were added only where they clarify neighboring concepts.

Potential but weak edges — for example linking every AI concept to [[Complex system]] or every LLM concept to [[Entropy]] — were deliberately rejected as graph noise.

== Finding 2 — one false semantic alias ==

[[Information]] contained this reader-facing link:

<pre>
[[Data structure|Data]]
</pre>

That rendered the general concept “Data” as an alias for [[Data structure]].

This was incorrect:

<pre>
data ≠ data structure
</pre>

The sentence now keeps “Data” as ordinary text and separately explains that, in computing, [[Data structure|data structures]] organize data without being identical to data itself.

No new [[Data]] stub was created.

== Finding 3 — provenance needed stronger publication-state labeling ==

The conceptual claims in Wave 8 remained sound, but several recent references needed clearer provenance.

=== AI agent ===

The article now names:

* NIST, “Agentic AI” (current 2026 institutional overview);
* NIST CAISI, “Announcing the AI Agent Standards Initiative for Interoperable and Secure Innovation” (17 February 2026);
* Lei Wang et al., 2024 autonomous-agent survey;
* Chowa et al., ''Artificial Intelligence Review'' 59, article 71 (2026), DOI 10.1007/s10462-025-11471-9.

This preserves the Wave 8 judgment:

<pre>
AI agent = Supported
</pre>

because the system category is real and institutionally recognized while taxonomy remains unsettled.

=== Tool use (artificial intelligence) ===

The bibliography now identifies:

* Xu et al., ''Data Science and Engineering'' 10 (2025), 533–563, DOI 10.1007/s41019-025-00296-9;
* Xinzhe Li, COLING 2025, pp. 9760–9779;
* Chowa et al. (2026).

This better supports the distinction:

<pre>
tool use ≠ function calling only
</pre>

=== Agent memory (artificial intelligence) ===

The three rapidly evolving survey sources are now explicitly labeled as preprints:

* Hu et al., arXiv:2512.13564 (2025 preprint);
* Cherepanov et al., arXiv:2412.06531 (2024 preprint);
* Du, arXiv:2603.07670 (2026 preprint).

This avoids presenting active taxonomy work as more settled than it is and supports retaining:

<pre>
Agent memory (artificial intelligence) = Supported
</pre>

rather than Established.

=== Large language model ===

The article now names Bommasani et al., ''On the Opportunities and Risks of Foundation Models'' (Stanford CRFM / arXiv:2108.07258) to strengthen:

<pre>
LLM ≠ foundation model by identity
</pre>

while retaining Vaswani et al. only as support for the dominant Transformer architecture, not the definition of all LLMs.

== Finding 4 — Wave 9 source specificity could be improved without changing semantics ==

Several broad Wave 9 pages used generic source-family labels.

The audit strengthened specific references while preserving article scope:

* [[Entropy]] now explicitly includes SEP “Information Processing and Thermodynamic Entropy” alongside Shannon, Cover/Thomas, and statistical mechanics.
* [[Feedback]] now names Åström & Murray, ''Feedback Systems'' (2008), rather than relying only on generic control-system literature.
* [[Self-organization]] now names Camazine et al., ''Self-Organization in Biological Systems'' (2001).
* [[Complex system]] now names Holland, ''Hidden Order'' (1995).
* [[Adaptation (systems)]] now names Holland, ''Hidden Order'' (1995).

No epistemic-status changes were required.

== Cross-wave semantic audit ==

=== Wave 7 → Wave 8 ===

[[Machine learning]] remains a method family within broader [[Artificial intelligence]].

[[Large language model]] remains a learned model class rather than the definition of machine learning.

[[AI agent]] remains a compound system concept and does not retroactively redefine machine learning.

=== Wave 7 → Wave 9 ===

[[Generalization (machine learning)]] remains distinct from [[Robustness]].

A model can generalize in-distribution without being robust to defined perturbations.

[[Distribution shift]] identifies changed data-generating conditions.

[[Adaptation (systems)]] identifies system change in response to conditions.

[[Robustness]] identifies preservation of specified function under perturbation.

These remain three different concepts.

[[Spurious correlation]] remains a relation/data issue rather than robustness itself; robustness testing can reveal its consequences.

=== Wave 8 → Wave 9 ===

[[Intelligent agent]], [[AI agent]], and [[Autonomous agent (artificial intelligence)]] can operate through [[Feedback]], but feedback is not sufficient for agenthood.

[[Adaptation (systems)]] can occur in agents without defining all agents.

[[Multi-agent system]] can be represented as an interaction [[Network]] and can exhibit [[Complex system|complex-system]] behavior, but it is not synonymous with either concept.

[[Agent memory (artificial intelligence)]] stores or reconstructs selected [[Information]], but information is broader than memory.

=== Information / entropy boundary ===

The Wave 9 distinction remains intact:

<pre>
Shannon entropy
= probabilistic uncertainty measure

thermodynamic/statistical entropy
= physical/statistical-mechanical quantity over physical ensembles
</pre>

The forms are mathematically related but not declared to be one identical physical quantity.

